1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,542
Chapter five — design internals.

2
00:00:03,602 --> 00:00:13,618
So far a node has been one
box with dials. Open it up.

3
00:00:13,678 --> 00:00:21,120
This is the device registry — a
Postgres node — from the inside.

4
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:29,124
The primitives on the left are what a
relational engine actually contains.

5
00:00:29,184 --> 00:00:35,925
Tables, indexes, procedures,
caches — not generic shapes.

6
00:00:35,985 --> 00:00:39,527
It is empty, so let us build one.

7
00:00:39,587 --> 00:00:44,579
An input — the inbound lookup.

8
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:49,647
A read cache in front of it.

9
00:00:49,707 --> 00:00:54,690
An index on device id.

10
00:00:54,750 --> 00:00:59,728
The table the rows actually live in.

11
00:00:59,788 --> 00:01:05,075
And an output — what leaves the node.

12
00:01:05,135 --> 00:01:27,391
Five entities. Now wire the read path.

13
00:01:27,451 --> 00:01:39,546
Lookup, cache, index, table, result
— the read path as it really runs.

14
00:01:39,606 --> 00:01:47,550
Each entity is modelled too — how
many entries, and what a lookup costs.

15
00:01:47,610 --> 00:01:57,553
The execution context is already computing:
critical path, inner ceiling, storage.

16
00:01:57,613 --> 00:02:05,678
And where the model is
not enough, you add code.

17
00:02:05,738 --> 00:02:25,675
Every entity takes a simulation function: input
and context in, a value and a latency out.

18
00:02:25,735 --> 00:02:33,483
That function runs instead of the
built-in maths for this entity.

19
00:02:33,543 --> 00:02:42,486
Or press Generate, and Claude writes
it from the entity it is attached to.

20
00:02:42,546 --> 00:02:47,463
Then run it.

21
00:02:47,523 --> 00:03:01,965
Two hundred ticks through the design you
just built — each entity using its own model.

22
00:03:02,025 --> 00:03:12,467
There is a node-level override too: replace
the whole node’s maths in one function.

23
00:03:12,527 --> 00:03:25,183
Or describe the objective and let Build
with AI lay the internals out for you.

24
00:03:25,243 --> 00:03:29,784
A node is a model. Inside it, another model —

25
00:03:29,844 --> 00:03:34,247
and where you disagree with it, your code.
